{"name":"Skeletor’s Cape","hex":"#773399","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cape","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A piece or point of land, extending beyond the adjacent coast into a sea or lake; a promontory; a headland."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sleeveless garment or part of a garment, hanging from the neck over the back, arms, and shoulders.","A superhero."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cape"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cape","blocks":[{"text":"A cape is a clothing accessory or a sleeveless outer garment of any length that hangs loosely and connects either at the neck or shoulders. They usually cover the back, shoulders, and arms. They come in a variety of styles and have been used throughout history for many different reasons."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cape"},{"title":"Skeletor","blocks":[{"text":"Skeletor is a supervillain and the main antagonist of the Masters of the Universe media franchise created by Mattel. The character first appeared in the minicomic He-Man and the Power Sword (1981), which was included with the original Masters of the Universe action figures. Skeletor is usually depicted as a skull-faced, blue-skinned sorcerer who serves as the archenemy of He-Man. As the self-proclaimed \"Evil Lord of Destruction\", Skeletor leads his Evil Warriors from his lair on Snake Mountain in his obsessive quest to unlock the secrets of Castle Grayskull, which he believes will give him the power to conquer the planet Eternia and the entire universe."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/01/SkeletorInfobox.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Skeletor"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Batman_and_Robin_1966.JPG/500px-Batman_and_Robin_1966.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia